{"v":1,"book":"gita","n":17,"title":"Threefold faith","narrator":{"name":"Sonia","voice":"en-GB-SoniaNeural"},"duration":277.8,"scenes":[{"layout":"title","headline":"Threefold Faith","visual":["You are what you believe in"],"L":[],"say":"Chapter Seventeen. Threefold Faith. What we believe in, Krishna says, shapes who we become.","start":0.0,"at":0.576,"end":5.088,"words":[[0.1,0.5,"Chapter"],[0.613,0.825,"Seventeen"],[1.8,0.75,"Threefold"],[2.562,0.575,"Faith"],[3.538,0.225,"What"]]},{"layout":"story","headline":"Faith without the rule book","visual":["What of those with faith","Who do not follow the scriptures?","Goodness, passion, or ignorance?"],"L":[],"say":"Arjuna asks a sincere question. What about people who practise with faith, but without following the scriptures? Is their faith in goodness, in passion, or in ignorance? Krishna answers that faith itself comes in three kinds, according to each person's nature.","start":5.088,"at":5.664,"end":23.568,"words":[[0.138,0.6,"Arjuna"],[0.75,0.375,"asks"],[1.137,0.062,"a"],[1.212,0.487,"sincere"],[1.712,0.637,"question"],[2.75,0.2,"What"],[2.962,0.35,"about"],[3.325,0.375,"people"],[3.712,0.125,"who"],[3.85,0.525,"practise"],[4.388,0.163,"with"],[4.562,0.487,"faith"],[5.325,0.163,"but"],[5.5,0.362,"without"],[5.875,0.4,"following"],[6.287,0.087,"the"],[6.388,0.725,"scriptures"],[7.487,0.163,"Is"],[7.662,0.163,"their"],[7.838,0.362,"faith"],[8.213,0.138,"in"],[8.363,0.588,"goodness"],[9.137,0.138,"in"],[9.287,0.55,"passion"],[10.062,0.125,"or"],[10.2,0.113,"in"],[10.325,0.75,"ignorance"],[11.438,0.487,"Krishna"],[11.938,0.487,"answers"],[12.438,0.2,"that"],[12.65,0.312,"faith"],[12.975,0.412,"itself"],[13.4,0.287,"comes"],[13.7,0.125,"in"],[13.838,0.25,"three"],[14.1,0.525,"kinds"],[14.887,0.4,"according"],[15.3,0.125,"to"],[15.438,0.25,"each"],[15.7,0.45,"person's"],[16.163,0.512,"nature"]]},{"layout":"verse","headline":"","visual":[],"L":["L1"],"ref":"17.03","verse":"O Arjuna, the faith of each is in accordance with one’s own natural disposition governed by Karmic impressions. One is known by one’s faith. One can become whatever one wants to be — if one constantly contemplates the object of desire with faith.","key":true,"vs":[2,45],"say":"Verse three. O Arjuna, the faith of each is in accordance with one’s own natural disposition governed by Karmic impressions. One is known by one’s faith. One can become whatever one wants to be — if one constantly contemplates the object of desire with faith.","start":23.568,"at":24.144,"end":42.336,"words":[[0.113,0.438,"Verse"],[0.562,0.463,"three"],[1.4,0.2,"O"],[1.613,0.613,"Arjuna"],[2.513,0.087,"the"],[2.612,0.3,"faith"],[2.925,0.113,"of"],[3.05,0.287,"each"],[3.35,0.1,"is"],[3.462,0.087,"in"],[3.562,0.575,"accordance"],[4.15,0.138,"with"],[4.3,0.35,"one’s"],[4.662,0.2,"own"],[4.875,0.388,"natural"],[5.275,0.725,"disposition"],[6.013,0.425,"governed"],[6.45,0.138,"by"],[6.6,0.425,"Karmic"],[7.037,0.775,"impressions"],[8.213,0.225,"One"],[8.45,0.15,"is"],[8.613,0.338,"known"],[8.963,0.188,"by"],[9.162,0.388,"one’s"],[9.562,0.525,"faith"],[10.488,0.263,"One"],[10.762,0.175,"can"],[10.95,0.375,"become"],[11.338,0.4,"whatever"],[11.75,0.25,"one"],[12.012,0.275,"wants"],[12.3,0.1,"to"],[12.412,0.3,"be"],[12.825,0.15,"if"],[12.988,0.212,"one"],[13.213,0.613,"constantly"],[13.838,0.713,"contemplates"],[14.562,0.113,"the"],[14.688,0.425,"object"],[15.125,0.087,"of"],[15.225,0.45,"desire"],[15.688,0.163,"with"],[15.863,0.512,"faith"]]},{"layout":"story","headline":"Three kinds of food","visual":["Goodness: juicy, smooth, nourishing","Passion: bitter, sour, salty, burning","Ignorance: stale, tasteless, impure"],"L":["L2"],"say":"Even food, Krishna says, comes in three kinds. People of goodness like food that is juicy, smooth and nourishing, food that brings long life, health and joy. People of passion like food that is very bitter, sour, salty, hot and burning, which brings pain and disease. And people of ignorance like food that is stale, tas