ng","Passion: unwillingly, or for a return","Ignorance: wrong time, wrong place, with contempt"],"L":["L2"],"say":"Even charity has three faces. Giving in goodness is done as a duty, at the right time and place, to someone worthy, expecting nothing back. Giving in ignorance is done at the wrong time and place, to the unworthy, or with disrespect.","start":104.28,"at":104.856,"end":121.056,"words":[[0.1,0.362,"Even"],[0.475,0.588,"charity"],[1.075,0.275,"has"],[1.363,0.263,"three"],[1.637,0.7,"faces"],[2.712,0.325,"Giving"],[3.05,0.113,"in"],[3.175,0.512,"goodness"],[3.7,0.15,"is"],[3.862,0.225,"done"],[4.1,0.113,"as"],[4.225,0.075,"a"],[4.312,0.5,"duty"],[5.025,0.138,"at"],[5.175,0.087,"the"],[5.275,0.287,"right"],[5.575,0.25,"time"],[5.838,0.113,"and"],[5.963,0.45,"place"],[6.662,0.1,"to"],[6.775,0.362,"someone"],[7.15,0.463,"worthy"],[7.8,0.588,"expecting"],[8.4,0.312,"nothing"],[8.725,0.463,"back"],[9.588,0.3,"Giving"],[9.9,0.1,"in"],[10.012,0.55,"ignorance"],[10.575,0.163,"is"],[10.75,0.225,"done"],[10.988,0.1,"at"],[11.1,0.1,"the"],[11.213,0.263,"wrong"],[11.488,0.3,"time"],[11.8,0.113,"and"],[11.925,0.487,"place"],[12.688,0.1,"to"],[12.8,0.113,"the"],[12.925,0.65,"unworthy"],[13.787,0.087,"or"],[13.887,0.212,"with"],[14.113,0.85,"disrespect"]]},{"layout":"verse","headline":"","visual":[],"L":["L2"],"ref":"17.21","verse":"Charity that is given unwillingly, or to get something in return, or to gain some fruit, is said to be in the mode of passion.","key":true,"vs":[9,34],"say":"And in between sits giving in passion. Verse twenty-one. Charity that is given unwillingly, or to get something in return, or to gain some fruit, is said to be in the mode of passion.","start":121.056,"at":121.632,"end":134.808,"words":[[0.138,0.15,"And"],[0.3,0.15,"in"],[0.463,0.438,"between"],[0.912,0.388,"sits"],[1.312,0.325,"giving"],[1.65,0.113,"in"],[1.775,0.588,"passion"],[2.725,0.425,"Verse"],[3.163,0.825,"twenty-one"],[4.362,0.588,"Charity"],[4.963,0.188,"that"],[5.162,0.125,"is"],[5.3,0.3,"given"],[5.612,0.7,"unwillingly"],[6.513,0.138,"or"],[6.662,0.138,"to"],[6.812,0.2,"get"],[7.025,0.338,"something"],[7.375,0.087,"in"],[7.475,0.537,"return"],[8.213,0.113,"or"],[8.338,0.138,"to"],[8.488,0.237,"gain"],[8.738,0.212,"some"],[8.963,0.412,"fruit"],[9.662,0.1,"is"],[9.775,0.225,"said"],[10.012,0.087,"to"],[10.113,0.138,"be"],[10.262,0.1,"in"],[10.375,0.075,"the"],[10.463,0.25,"mode"],[10.725,0.113,"of"],[10.85,0.525,"passion"]]},{"layout":"story","headline":"OM TAT SAT","visual":["OM: every sacred act begins with it","TAT: done without seeking reward","SAT: reality, goodness, and faith itself"],"L":[],"say":"Krishna ends with the threefold name of God: OM TAT SAT. Sacred acts begin with OM. TAT, meaning He is all, is spoken by those who act without seeking a reward. And SAT means reality and goodness. Faith in sacrifice, charity and discipline is itself called SAT.","start":134.808,"at":135.384,"end":155.088,"words":[[0.1,0.487,"Krishna"],[0.6,0.338,"ends"],[0.95,0.138,"with"],[1.1,0.087,"the"],[1.2,0.562,"threefold"],[1.775,0.212,"name"],[2.0,0.113,"of"],[2.125,0.338,"God"],[2.737,0.275,"OM"],[3.025,0.3,"TAT"],[3.337,0.388,"SAT"],[4.362,0.388,"Sacred"],[4.763,0.3,"acts"],[5.075,0.287,"begin"],[5.375,0.15,"with"],[5.537,0.275,"OM."],[5.825,0.688,"TAT"],[6.825,0.275,"meaning"],[7.112,0.125,"He"],[7.25,0.125,"is"],[7.388,0.287,"all"],[7.875,0.087,"is"],[7.975,0.45,"spoken"],[8.438,0.138,"by"],[8.588,0.287,"those"],[8.887,0.113,"who"],[9.012,0.3,"act"],[9.325,0.312,"without"],[9.65,0.35,"seeking"],[10.012,0.05,"a"],[10.075,0.562,"reward"],[11.037,0.163,"And"],[11.213,0.4,"SAT"],[11.625,0.3,"means"],[11.938,0.662,"reality"],[12.613,0.163,"and"],[12.787,0.688,"goodness"],[13.863,0.388,"Faith"],[14.262,0.138,"in"],[14.412,0.825,"sacrifice"],[15.475,0.613,"charity"],[16.175,0.138,"and"],[16.325,0.625,"discipline"],[16.962,0.163,"is"],[17.137,0.487,"itself"],[17.637,0.287,"called"],[17.938,0.537,"SAT"]]},{"layout":"verse","headline":"","visual":[],"L":["L4"],"ref":"17.28","verse":"Whatever is done without faith — whether it is sacrifice, charity, austerity, or any other act — is called ‘ASAT’. It has no value here or hereafter, O Arjuna.","key":true,"vs":[9,38],"say":"Which leads to the chapter's final verse. Verse twenty-eight. Whatever is done without faith — whether it is sacrifice, charity, austerity, or any other act — is called ‘ASAT’. It has no value here or hereafter, O Arjuna.","start":155.088,"at":155.664,"end":172.944,"words":[[0.138,0.25,"Which"],[0.4,0.4,"leads"],[0.812,0.1,"to"],[0.925,0.113,"the"],[1.05,0.55,"chapter's"],[1.613,0.362,"final"],[1.988,0.562,"verse"],[2.938,0.362,"Verse"],[3.312,0.875,"twenty-eight"],[4.588,0.45,"Whatever"],[5.05,0.138,"is"],[5.2,0.25,"done"],[5.463,0.35,"without"],[5.825,0.487,"faith"],[6.412,0.237,"whether"],[6.662,0.113,"it"],[6.787,0.113,"is"],[6.912,0.762,"sacrifice"],[7.925,0.6,"charity"],[8.725,0.7,"austerity"],[9.688,0.163,"or"],[9.863,0.2,"any"],[10.075,0.237,"other"],[10.325,0.388,"act"],[10.825,0.1,"is"],[10.938,0.312,"called"],[11.262,0.625,"ASAT"],[12.287,0.113,"It"],[12.412,0.188,"has"],[12.613,0.188,"no"],[12.812,0.4,"value"],[13.225,0.375,"here"],[13.613,0.1,"or"],[13.725,0.762,"hereafter"],[14.7,0.138,"O"],[14.85,0.613,"Arjuna"]]},{"layout":"lesson","headline":"Faith Is Shaped by One's Dominant Mode of Nature","visual":["Faith follows one's nature","One is known by one's faith","We become what we hold with faith"],"L":["L1"],"say":"Lesson one. Faith is shaped by one's dominant mode of nature. Those in goodness worship the divine; those in passion worship power; those in ignorance worship ghosts and spirits. One is known by one's faith, and over time, we become what we believe in.","start":172.944,"at":173.52,"end":191.472,"words":[[0.125,0.45,"Lesson"],[0.588,0.45,"one"],[1.413,0.412,"Faith"],[1.837,0.138,"is"],[1.988,0.463,"shaped"],[2.462,0.163,"by"],[2.638,0.375,"one's"],[3.025,0.487,"dominant"],[3.525,0.25,"mode"],[3.788,0.113,"of"],[3.913,0.55,"nature"],[4.862,0.312,"Those"],[5.188,0.125,"in"],[5.325,0.487,"goodness"],[5.825,0.45,"worship"],[6.287,0.087,"the"],[6.388,0.5,"divine"],[7.2,0.25,"those"],[7.463,0.113,"in"],[7.588,0.438,"passion"],[8.037,0.425,"worship"],[8.475,0.425,"power"],[9.2,0.225,"those"],[9.438,0.1,"in"],[9.55,0.475,"ignorance"],[10.037,0.475,"worship"],[10.525,0.45,"ghosts"],[10.988,0.125,"and"],[11.125,0.7,"spirits"],[12.225,0.237,"One"],[12.475,0.138,"is"],[12.625,0.287,"known"],[12.925,0.175,"by"],[13.113,0.338,"one's"],[13.463,0.463,"faith"],[14.15,0.113,"and"],[14.275,0.225,"over"],[14.512,0.425,"time"],[15.213,0.125,"we"],[15.35,0.388,"become"],[15.75,0.2,"what"],[15.963,0.1,"we"],[16.075,0.362,"believe"],[16.45,0.275,"in"]]},{"layout":"lesson","headline":"Food, Sacrifice, Austerity, and Charity Each Have Three Modes","visual":["Food, sacrifice, austerity, charity","Each takes on the quality behind it","Goodness, passion or ignorance"],"L":["L2"],"say":"Lesson two. Food, sacrifice, austerity and charity each have three modes. Every spiritual act takes on the quality of the force behind it. The same gift, the same fast, the same prayer can be done in goodness, in passion or in ignorance. The motive makes the difference.","start":191.472,"at":192.048,"end":212.424,"words":[[0.113,0.463,"Lesson"],[0.588,0.463,"two"],[1.438,0.475,"Food"],[2.175,0.812,"sacrifice"],[3.188,0.738,"austerity"],[4.013,0.15,"and"],[4.175,0.6,"charity"],[4.787,0.25,"each"],[5.05,0.175,"have"],[5.237,0.237,"three"],[5.487,0.55,"modes"],[6.412,0.312,"Every"],[6.737,0.688,"spiritual"],[7.438,0.425,"act"],[7.875,0.312,"takes"],[8.2,0.1,"on"],[8.312,0.075,"the"],[8.4,0.562,"quality"],[8.975,0.125,"of"],[9.113,0.087,"the"],[9.213,0.35,"force"],[9.575,0.412,"behind"],[10.0,0.338,"it"],[10.738,0.113,"The"],[10.863,0.3,"same"],[11.175,0.45,"gift"],[11.825,0.087,"the"],[11.925,0.3,"same"],[12.238,0.525,"fast"],[13.037,0.087,"the"],[13.137,0.275,"same"],[13.425,0.375,"prayer"],[13.812,0.138,"can"],[13.963,0.1,"be"],[14.075,0.2,"done"],[14.287,0.113,"in"],[14.412,0.55,"goodness"],[15.188,0.125,"in"],[15.325,0.55,"passion"],[15.975,0.125,"or"],[16.113,0.1,"in"],[16.225,0.662,"ignorance"],[17.288,0.1,"The"],[17.4,0.525,"motive"],[17.938,0.338,"makes"],[18.288,0.113,"the"],[18.413,0.738,"difference"]]},{"layout":"lesson","headline":"Austerity Has Three Dimensions — Deed, Word, and Thought","visual":["Of deed: purity, honesty, nonviolence","Of word: truthful, kind, beneficial","Of thought: serenity, gentleness, self-control"],"L":["L3"],"say":"Lesson three. Austerity has three dimensions: deed, word and thought. In deed: purity, honesty, nonviolence and service to the wise. In word: speech that is truthful, kind, pleasant and helpful. In thought: serenity, gentleness and self-control. Discipline is not punishment. It is refinement.","start":212.424,"at":213.0,"end":238.104,"words":[[0.113,0.475,"Lesson"],[0.6,0.512,"three"],[1.512,0.7,"Austerity"],[2.225,0.25,"has"],[2.487,0.212,"three"],[2.712,0.812,"dimensions"],[3.837,0.388,"deed"],[4.425,0.425,"word"],[4.95,0.138,"and"],[5.1,0.55,"thought"],[6.025,0.188,"In"],[6.225,0.4,"deed"],[6.925,0.613,"purity"],[7.763,0.562,"honesty"],[8.588,0.838,"nonviolence"],[9.525,0.125,"and"],[9.662,0.475,"service"],[10.15,0.1,"to"],[10.262,0.087,"the"],[10.363,0.562,"wise"],[11.325,0.15,"In"],[11.488,0.425,"word"],[12.238,0.412,"speech"],[12.662,0.163,"that"],[12.838,0.125,"is"],[12.975,0.613,"truthful"],[13.787,0.487,"kind"],[14.525,0.5,"pleasant"],[15.037,0.1,"and"],[15.15,0.588,"helpful"],[16.137,0.175,"In"],[16.325,0.463,"thought"],[17.087,0.725,"serenity"],[18.087,0.725,"gentleness"],[18.913,0.138,"and"],[19.062,0.887,"self-control"],[20.312,0.688,"Discipline"],[21.012,0.175,"is"],[21.2,0.263,"not"],[21.475,0.812,"punishment"],[22.663,0.163,"It"],[22.837,0.15,"is"],[23.0,0.875,"refinement"]]},{"layout":"lesson","headline":"Action Without Faith Has No Spiritual Value","visual":["Sacrifice, charity or austerity without faith","Is called asat","Faith turns an outer act into a spiritual one"],"L":["L4"],"say":"Lesson four. Action without faith has no spiritual value. Whatever is done without faith, whether sacrifice, charity or austerity, is called asat, unreal. It brings nothing here or hereafter. Faith is what turns an outer act into an inner one.","start":238.104,"at":238.68,"end":257.592,"words":[[0.138,0.438,"Lesson"],[0.588,0.463,"four"],[1.413,0.525,"Action"],[1.95,0.375,"without"],[2.337,0.45,"faith"],[2.8,0.237,"has"],[3.05,0.175,"no"],[3.237,0.588,"spiritual"],[3.837,0.525,"value"],[4.75,0.45,"Whatever"],[5.213,0.138,"is"],[5.362,0.237,"done"],[5.612,0.338,"without"],[5.963,0.487,"faith"],[6.675,0.225,"whether"],[6.912,0.787,"sacrifice"],[7.912,0.6,"charity"],[8.6,0.125,"or"],[8.738,0.7,"austerity"],[9.738,0.125,"is"],[9.875,0.338,"called"],[10.225,0.562,"asat"],[10.963,0.588,"unreal"],[11.95,0.163,"It"],[12.125,0.338,"brings"],[12.475,0.388,"nothing"],[12.875,0.388,"here"],[13.275,0.113,"or"],[13.4,0.812,"hereafter"],[14.6,0.412,"Faith"],[15.025,0.125,"is"],[15.162,0.225,"what"],[15.4,0.325,"turns"],[15.738,0.113,"an"],[15.863,0.4,"outer"],[16.275,0.35,"act"],[16.637,0.287,"into"],[16.938,0.113,"an"],[17.062,0.212,"inner"],[17.288,0.4,"one"]]},{"layout":"closing","headline":"Faith gives the act its worth","visual":["You are what your faith is","Food, speech, giving: all have three modes","Without faith, an act is empty"],"L":[],"say":"So, Chapter Seventeen. We are what our faith is. Food, discipline, speech and giving all come in three modes, and the force behind them decides their worth. Without faith, even a great act is empty. Next, the final chapter: the whole Gita, drawn together.","start":257.592,"at":258.168,"end":277.8,"words":[[0.125,0.45,"So"],[0.85,0.425,"Chapter"],[1.288,0.8,"Seventeen"],[2.487,0.188,"We"],[2.688,0.087,"are"],[2.788,0.275,"what"],[3.075,0.138,"our"],[3.225,0.362,"faith"],[3.6,0.4,"is"],[4.388,0.512,"Food"],[5.125,0.6,"discipline"],[5.938,0.512,"speech"],[6.55,0.1,"and"],[6